{"chunk_id": "fbe11eaf692b", "text": "After Drona\u2019s death, his son Ashwatthama burns with grief and shame, declaring that he will annihilate the Panchalas to repay the debt he owes his slain father. In a fierce speech to the Kauravas, he condemns his own strength and weapons for failing to protect Drona and vows terrible vengeance. He reveals the secret of the Narayana weapon, a divine missile granted to Drona by Lord Narayana with strict conditions: it is unstoppable and must not be used rashly or against defenseless foes. Determined to unleash it, Ashwatthama invokes the weapon. Terrifying cosmic omens follow\u2014winds rage, mountains split, rivers reverse, and darkness spreads\u2014striking fear in gods and warriors alike. As the Kaurava army rallies around him, the Pandavas prepare to respond to the catastrophic divine weapon now unleashed upon the battlefield.\nAshwatthama vows vengeance for Drona\u2019s death and invokes the terrifying Narayana weapon, causing cosmic disturbances that alarm both armies.\nThemes: filial vengeance, divine weapons, cosmic omens, war fury, duty to father", "vector": [-0.010690153576433659, -0.012841759249567986, -0.007072469685226679, 0.004367690999060869, -0.006970658898353577, 0.016778450459241867, -0.03730354458093643, -0.0159639623016119, -0.021882575005292892, 0.0024757038336247206, 0.024516085162758827, 0.01343226246535778, 0.00664486363530159, 0.021380307152867317, 0.011090610176324844, 0.01367660891264677, 0.050471097230911255, -0.014348560944199562, 0.021814700216054916, -0.02655230462551117, -0.0003124324430245906, -0.01085983868688345, -0.0055113681592047215, 0.027258194983005524, -0.013452624902129173, 0.01326257735490799, 0.0032800105400383472, -0.043195005506277084, 0.013730907812714577, -0.015896087512373924, 0.0006070479867048562, -0.006000060588121414, 0.0016069166595116258, 0.006970658898353577, -0.03461573272943497, 0.007574737071990967, -0.00253169983625412, -0.027516115456819534, 0.010995586402714252, -0